  "agent": {
    "note": "**v1 PROD GATE — `@m0saic/dsl-tutorial/v1` \"DSL Tutorial\"** (gate 33 — the north-star polish benchmark; load-bearing since gate 30 deprecated the animated wireframe in its favour; chart: `.ai/LAUNCH/v1-template-cut.md`). Core tier, tags dsl-tutorial · tutorial · wireframe · docs · animated. Props = pure defaults → the 2×2 walk, light preset, **15.8s natural** (was 12s: see finding 1).\n\nYour heads-up (\"text clipping — we should have debug layout guards\") drove the pre-audit. The engine's drawtext never shrinks a string (`fit:\"contain\"` only picks the anchor), and every font in the tutorial scaled from the bar HEIGHT alone — so anything narrower than 16:9 clipped: on 1080×1920 the title read \"Animated\", the pills \"ed 1\" / \"p 10 /\", the inspector \"INSF\" / \"60\" (for 960) / \"80\" (for 1080) / \"ENGIN\", and every status metric was cut mid-word.\n\n| Stage | Current | Proposed |\n|---|---|---|\n| Flags | core · not internal · not deprecated | confirm |\n| Label | \"DSL Tutorial\" | keep |\n| Header title default | was \"Animated Wireframe\" (the deprecated sibling's name) | **\"DSL Tutorial\"** — revertable, one line |\n| Duration | the 12s outputHint was read as a PIN → every walk crammed/stretched to 12s (default ran at 1.3×; the gallery preview's 61-step walk at 4.7×) | **Q1 law**: only an explicit ask pins (CLI `--durationMs`, Make Duration). Unpinned = the walk's natural length authored on `durationMs` (~0.9s/char at 1×); the Speed pill reads 1.0× |\n| Cover / Tutorial | none / none | none / none (the template IS a tutorial) |\n| Previews | 07-02 set: \"Animated Wireframe\" header, 4.7× crammed walk, strip clipped at both ends | RE-MINT after the verdict (+ corner-M) |\n| Battery | `.scratch/claude/dsl-tutorial-gate-battery.mjs` — **29/29** (23 CLI renders + ffprobe/pixel asserts: natural / pinned / speed durations, 0 audio streams ×23, dark vs light, strip edge columns ink-free, tiny auto-hide + compact pills, portrait app-bar chrome) | — |\n| Contract sweep | `debugLayout` holds (0 violations) at 1920×1080 · 1280×720 · 1080×1920 · 1080×1080 · 3840×2160 · 960×540 · 800×450 · 704×396 · 640×360 · 480×270 · 320×180 · 1920×200, plus the 100-tile grid, overlay + passthrough layouts, a long title | — |\n\n**Pre-audit findings → fixed:**\n\n| Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| ⭐ **Text clipped at any non-16:9 canvas** (portrait / square / tiny): title, both pills, inspector caption + chips + 4-digit values + section caption, every status metric | Every string is WIDTH-FITTED under a CLI width model (`_shared/text-fit.ts`, the alpine pack's `textEmUnits × em` ruler — the SAME ruler the contract checks with): the bar height picks the design size, the cell caps it, floors are explicit. Degrade ladders instead of clips: the title ellipsizes at 70% of its design size · pills drop to compact wording (`1.0x` · `10 / 16`) · the status strip drops trailing metrics · inspector captions blank at the floor · tile dims lines drop when they can't fit at 9px |\n| ⭐ **No `debugLayout` guard** | `debugLayout` runs `withLayoutContract` THROUGH the nested panels (checkLayout flattens the children): `textFits` on 11 labels (header-title / header-pill / status-label / metric-label / metric-value / narration / inspector-title / chip / field-label / field-value / section-title), each with the em its fit used. On → the contract wireframe (green = the measured rule) |\n| DSL strip: edge glyphs sat half a column from the panel edge; the flat 1.6·cellW font cap let `>` (.86em) overlap its neighbours and clip at both ends | the column font is bounded by the WIDEST glyph in the string under a per-glyph m0 model (no overlap, no edge clip); ruler labels likewise |\n| Narration font was height-only → ran off the right edge on portrait | one font fits the LONGEST line; still-overflowing lines ellipsize at the 10px floor |\n| Chrome rows were % of HEIGHT → a 173px header slab on portrait | rows size off `min(H, 0.75·W)` — landscape byte-identical (9/9/6/70/6), portrait/square get app-bar chrome and hand the rest to the body |\n| Inspector rows filled the panel height → 140px rows with small text on portrait | rows capped at 30% of the panel width, slack at the bottom |\n| ⭐ **480×270 CRASHED** (\"expects 39 renderable sources but doc.sources has 40\"): the inspector's section rule = 1/11 of a ~9px band → a 0-size frame | the rule is quantized at ≥2.5px per unit (a hairline the engine can't zero), captions only below 7px; AND the inspector auto-hides under a 140px slot (canvases < 700px wide — its 3px cells were never legible) |\n| The contract ITSELF found two more during the sweep: the whole nested layout collapsed (flatten `SPLIT_EXCEEDS_AXIS`) between 700 and 960px wide, and a chip / a pill overshot by 1–2px at 800×450 / 960×540 — quantization eats an ABSOLUTE 1–2px per split level, not a proportional slice | fit budget = cell × 0.94 − 2px (`fitBudget`); 12-canvas sweep clean |\n| ⭐ **CLI `.mosaicx` path never told templates the ask** (`make` / `resolve` built the engine context WITHOUT userIntent): `--durationMs` and the wrapper's `durationMs` set the render length but the template kept its natural timeline → stress-01 rendered 30s of a 220s walk (TRUNCATED mid-walk, Speed 1.0×), while Make (which threads its Duration field) rendered the fit | CLI `mosaicxUserIntent` (packages/cli `mosaicxRunner.ts`, 3 locks): the render length reaches templates as userIntent on BOTH paths, so a frozen twin carries the same fitted timeline `make` renders. CLI == Make. (Every self-timing template on the mosaicx path gains this — subtitle-burn, highlights, search-typing…) |\n| Chips + narration blanked for the closing trail hold (the last step's window ended before the end; values + canvas held theirs) | the last step's chip / narration windows run to the end of the video |\n| No `format` / `audio` stamps (pre-convention) | `format:{video,mp4}` + `audio:{mode:\"off\"}` (+ `outputHints.format`); battery verifies 0 audio streams |\n| Registry description promised \"a debugger\" panel (folded into the inspector long ago) | rewritten to match the template |\n\n**Verified, no change needed:** camera auto-zoom + pull-back on the 100-tile grid · paged strip (243 chars, 3 pages) · overlay layouts take the per-tile z-ordered path · null + passthrough narration (\"donate 480px forward … claimed by the next tile\") · panel toggles fold their space into the body · `stepEvents:\"all\"` · numeric `1`/`0` input normalizes to `F`/`>` · 4K.\n\n**Design notes (not bugs):** portrait keeps the IDE shell side-by-side with the canvas letterboxed to its true shape (a stacked portrait layout is a v2 question) · the flattened `.mosaic` twin drops `effects.camera` (platform flatten), so zoomed stress twins show the fit-to-panel canvas — the `.mosaicx` recipes render the camera.\n\nLocks: 11 dsl-tutorial suites / 134 tests + 3 CLI (gate-33 file: contract sweep at 7 canvases + overlay layout + the 100-tile grid, duration law, stamps, degrade ladders, chrome unit, auto-hide, tiny-canvas parse). Stress ×10 pre-minted in `stress/` (agent pass clean; mid/end PNGs beside the recipes, mp4s local) — review after the default verdict.",
    "question": "Gate-33 verdict on the default (2×2 light, 15.8s natural, \"DSL Tutorial\" header) · flip Debug layout ON once to see the contract · then nudge: Duration (pins the walk), a portrait/square output, a long Title, a dense m0 — anything still clip? · core confirm. Then stress-01..10."
  },
